{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--information-disclosure--common-sources-of-information-disclosure--source-code-disclosure-via-backup-files","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/information-disclosure/common-sources-of-information-disclosure/source-code-disclosure-via-backup-files.md","title":"Source code disclosure via backup files","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/information-disclosure/common-sources-of-information-disclosure/source-code-disclosure-via-backup-files.md","html":"<h1 id=\"source-code-disclosure-via-backup-files\">Source code disclosure via backup files</h1>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab leaks its source code via backup files in a hidden directory. To solve the lab, identify and submit the database password, which is hard-coded in the leaked source code.</p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(22)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Checking source code page (CTRL+U) and discovering others pages there're not of interesting, so the idea is to try to guess a potential backup page (eg. git, backup).</p>\n<p>In this case i was lucky, because the correct directory path was backup: <a href=\"https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup</a></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(25)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>with the relative file .bak called: ProductTemplate.java.bak that contain a java package with relative DB information and the password/answer that we need to solve the lab.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup/ProductTemplate.java.bak\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(23)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup/ProductTemplate.java.bak\"></button><figcaption><p><a href=\"https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup/ProductTemplate.java.bak\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0a5400e703e5812285d9c2ef009700ba.web-security-academy.net/backup/ProductTemplate.java.bak</a></p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(24)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"Source code disclosure via backup files screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"Source code disclosure via backup files Description This lab leaks its source code via backup files in a hidden directory. To solve the lab, identify and submit the database password, which is hard-coded in the leaked so","searchText":"Description Solution"}